
## Requirements
- **OS**: Ubuntu 22.04 LTS
- **Machine Type**: t3.medium or equivalent
- **Memory**: 4GB RAM minimum
- **Storage**: 8GB
- **Network**: SSH (port 22), HTTP (port 5000)

## Automated Deployment

### Prerequisites
Install Ansible on your local machine:

sudo apt update && sudo apt install ansible -y


### Deploy (Completely Hands-Free)

1. **Download deployment files:**

   wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IamHermanto/traffic-simulation-deployment/main/deploy.yml

   wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IamHermanto/traffic-simulation-deployment/main/inventory.yml.template


2. **Configure server:**

   cp inventory.yml.template inventory.yml
   nano inventory.yml
   
   Update the following in `inventory.yml`:
   - Replace `your-server-hostname.com` with your actual server hostname
   - Replace `path/to/your/key.pem` with the path to your SSH key file

3. **Run deployment:**

   ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml deploy.yml
   

## Access

After deployment completes, the system is immediately accessible:

- **Web Dashboard**: `http://your-server:5000/dashboard`
- **API Status**: `http://your-server:5000/api/status`

## API Endpoints

### Check System Status
```
curl http://your-server:5000/api/status
curl http://your-server:5000/api/traffic/lights
```

### Control Operations

# Emergency stop (all red)
curl -X POST http://your-server:5000/api/traffic/lights/set_all_red

# Clear all intersections (all green)
curl -X POST http://your-server:5000/api/traffic/lights/set_all_green

# System test (randomize lights)
curl -X POST http://your-server:5000/api/traffic/lights/randomize

# Restore normal automatic operation
curl -X POST http://your-server:5000/api/traffic/system/restore


## Services

The system runs as systemd services that start automatically on boot:
- `unity-traffic.service` - Unity traffic simulation server
- `traffic-api.service` - Flask REST API server

Check service status:

sudo systemctl status unity-traffic
sudo systemctl status traffic-api
